course: dictionary
lesson: 13634
title: Industrialisation
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Industrialisation is the change from farming and handwork to factories, machines and big industry. Before it, most people made things by hand or grew food on the land. Then machines let work happen faster, in one place, and many more things could be made.
explain: «Rapid industrialisation turned quiet villages into busy towns in only a few decades.» Rapid means very fast, so the change happened quickly. The clues are quiet villages and busy towns: the places changed a lot.
explain: In history, the word often means the Industrial Revolution in Britain, which began around 1760 and then spread to Europe, North America and the world. Historians also call this period «the age of industrialisation».
fact: Industrialisation means a change from farming and handwork to factories, machines and big industry.
fact: The Industrial Revolution in Britain began from about 1760, then spread to Europe, North America and the world.
fact: Industrialisation brought steam engines, factories, railways and growing cities.
fact: Industrialisation also caused child labour, pollution and crowded housing.
fact: Many countries are still industrialising today. In US spelling it is «industrialization».
exercise: «Rapid industrialisation turned quiet villages into busy towns.» What does rapid mean? | Very slow | Very quiet | *Very fast | Very small
exercise: In history lessons, what does industrialisation mean? | A kind of old castle | *The change from farming and handwork to factories and machines | A type of steam engine | The change from cities back to the countryside
exercise: Which of these came with industrialisation? | Stone tools only | Castles built on hills | *Factories and railways | Cave paintings
test: In Britain, industrialisation began from about which year? | 1560 | *1760 | 1860 | 1960
test: What was one bad effect of industrialisation? | Open green fields for all | Clean rivers everywhere | Fewer machines | *Pollution, such as smoky air
exam: Explain in your own words what industrialisation means. | A new kind of school | A change from factories back to farms | A type of food | *A change from farming and handwork to factories, machines and big industry
